  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Policy Monitoring Research</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the 2009 PPA report and PCM meeting with Connect partners, it was clear that partners are engaging in advocacy and have done good work mobilising communities and developing strategies.  However, it was also clear that partners are missing the ability to develop a really solid evidence base for their advocacy positions. While partners are clearly building good relationships with decision makers, it is crucial to ensure that they have the evidence they need to support their arguments and influence for change. 

A clear resource for supporting partners in strengthening their understanding and capacity in this regard is the Policy Monitoring Toolkit (developed by Christian Aid, Trocaire, and CAFOD). It is intended to run a two-year project to facilitate Connect partners through the process of using the tool kit to give them and their constituents the skills for evidence gathering. The partners will then use these skills to carry out their own research project on their chosen issue. This will provide a practical focus both for partner advocacy and for CAFOD advocacy support over the next two years and the final stages of the Connect programme. 

This PSGA is to leverage resources to implement year 1 of this project whiles efforts are being made to raise resources for year 2.</narrative>
  </description>
